course: dictionary
lesson: 14948
title: Rejoin: join again, or reply
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word rejoin is made of two parts. Re- means again, and join means to come together. So to rejoin something is to join it again after being apart. «After her week in bed with flu, Mia rejoined the netball team.» The clues are after, in bed and back: Mia was away, and now she is with her team again.
explain: Rejoin can also mean to reply, often quickly or sharply. This is a formal use, so you will meet it mostly in stories. «"I am not going to bed yet," rejoined Sam.» Sam is answering someone who has just told him to go to bed. Ask yourself: did someone just say something? If they did, rejoined may mean replied.
explain: Use the words around the word to choose the meaning. If the sentence is about a team, a class, a group or a path, it usually means join again. If someone has just spoken and another person answers, it may mean reply. Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Rejoin means to join or meet again after being apart.
fact: Rejoin can also mean to reply, often quickly or sharply, in formal writing.
fact: The prefix re- means again, so rejoin starts with the idea of doing something once more.
fact: «Rejoin the group» means go back to the people you were with.
fact: «Rejoin the road» means get back onto the road after leaving it.
exercise: «After her illness, Mia rejoined the class on Monday.» What does rejoined mean here? | Argued with the teacher | *Came back to join the class again | Wrote a letter to the class | Left the class for good
exercise: «"Not a chance," rejoined Tom sharply.» What does rejoined mean here? | Stood up and walked off | Cried quietly | *Replied | Rejoined the group
exercise: «The walkers left the path to look at a stream, then rejoined it further on.» Which word could replace rejoined? | *returned to | ate | fell | hid
test: The prefix re- in rejoin means what? | Under | Before | Never | *Again
test: «"Let's go home," rejoined Lily.» What does rejoined mean? | Joined the home team again | Went to sleep | *Answered | Left the house
exam: «The dog ran off after the ball, but later rejoined its owner in the park.» Which meaning fits best? | Quarrelled with | Ran away for good | Fell asleep near | *Met up with again
